      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Correlations between coronary angiographic findings and the results of some noninvasive functional tests (electro- and echocardiography, bicycle ergometry, etc.) were examined in 50 patients. A relationship was established between the quantity of essentially (over 50% of the lumen) stenosed major coronary arteries and stress tolerance or the double product."},
